@startuml PropORACLE_Fetch_Pipeline
' Fetch apps and process — PrizePicks slate ingest
' Render: PlantUML extension or https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml

title PropORACLE — Fetch pipeline (step1)

actor Operator
actor "Task\nScheduler" as Sched
participant "run_daily.ps1\n/ refresh / late_fetch" as Orch
participant "Sport step1" as Step1
participant "prizepicks_cdp.py\n:9222" as CDP
participant "prizepicks_http.py\ncurl_cffi" as HTTP
participant "PrizePicks" as PP
participant "Stats APIs\nESPN / boxes" as Stats
participant "step2–8\nenrich + rank" as Enrich

Sched -> Orch : 9PM day-ahead / 1AM / 5AM\n8AM / 9 / 9:45 / 10:30 / 1PM / 4:30
Operator -> Orch : manual catchup
Orch -> Step1 : per sport (WNBA, MLB, Soccer,\nTennis, NFL, CFB, NBA…)

alt Chrome debug :9222 warm
  Step1 -> CDP : connect_over_cdp (30s attach)
  CDP -> PP : in-page fetch() + AbortController
  PP --> CDP : projections JSON
else HTTP fallback
  Step1 -> HTTP : curl_cffi (low retry budget)
  HTTP -> PP : projections
  PP --> HTTP : JSON (DataDome may hang)
end

Step1 -> Stats : player / game / defense
Stats --> Step1 : boxes, ranks, match logs
Step1 -> Enrich : step2 normalize … step7 ML … step8 direction
Enrich --> Orch : step8_*_direction_clean.xlsx\n(+ D2 copy to outputs/<date>/)

note right of CDP
  Soccer / Tennis / WNBA / MLB:
  CDP-first + --fail-fast.
  Late fetch: per-sport wall-clock kill
  so one board cannot block the rest.
end note

@enduml
